==Skins==
The current available Skins are:
*Vintage Skins (Completing all the [[Mastery]] quests of a [[Toon]]. Available for every playable Toon);
*Gamepass Skins (Buying from the Gamepass section for Robux from [[Dyle's Store]] in the lobby)
*Dyle's Store Skins (Buying with [[Ichor]] from the Skins section from [[Dyle's Store]] in the lobby)

Unobtainable Skins:
*{{HT|Christmas}}, [[Halloween Event|Halloween]], and {{HT|Easter}} Skins (buying from their respective Event Store's Skin section in the lobby during their respective event);
*Event [[Quest]] Skins (exclusive to the event in which they were released; for example, Christmas Quest Skins can only be obtained during the Christmas event);
*The [[Care Bears Collab]] Skins (limited to the time they were released).

NOTE: More Toon Skins will be added in the future.

===Skin Appearances and Obtainability===
*Vintage: The Vintage Skins are a gray-scale version of the normal model of the [[Toon]] with a pie-like pupil, sometimes wearing a different color scheme for already black and white Toons. This Skin type is available for every obtainable Toon. To get a Vintage Skin, you need to complete a Toon's [[Mastery]] to obtain it.
*[[Dyle's Store]]: Skins of varying themes, usually related to the respective Toon's personality, style, lore, etc. This Skin type is available for every obtainable Toon (excluding the [[Holiday Toons]]). You can buy them with {{TI|Ichor|name=true}} from Dyle's Store under the Skins category.
*[[Bobette's Store|Bobette's Christmas Shop]]: Skins of varying themes, typically related to/themed around Christmas. This Skin type is currently available for every Toon excluding {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}, {{CI|Squirm|name=true}}, {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, and [[Holiday Toons]] that aren't featured in the [[Christmas Event]]. This Skin type is limited and can only be obtained during the Christmas Event, from Bobette's Christmas Shop.
*[[Bassie's Store|Bassie's Easter Shop]]: Skins of varying themes, generally relating to the Easter holiday and spring themes. This Skin type is currently available for every Toon excluding Holiday Toons that aren't featured in the [[Easter Event]] and Waxwell. This Skin type is limited and can only be obtained during the Easter Event from Bassie's Easter Shop.
*[[Gourdy's Store|Gourdy's Halloween Shop]]: Skins of varying themes, generally relating to Halloween costumes or Day of the Dead. This Skin type is available for every obtainable Toon except for all the Holiday Toons not featured in the [[Halloween Event]]. This Skin type is limited and can only be obtained during the Halloween Event from Gourdy's Halloween Shop (on October 2nd).
*[[Cosmetic Packs]]: Skins that are obtainable by purchasing it under the Gamepasses section with {{Robux|40}} per Toon in the pack.
**[[Star-Time Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to stars and outer space, with color schemes of yellow, white, and navy blue. This Skin type is available for all base-game {{Type|Mains}} ([[Astro]], [[Pebble]], [[Shelly]], [[Sprout]], and [[Vee]]).
**[[Show-Time Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to circuses, featuring color schemes of red, dark blue, teal, and white. This Skin type is available for Circus Troupe Toons {{Small|({{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Looey|name=true}}, & Yatta)}}, {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, and {{CI|Vee|name=true}}.
**[[Snow-Time Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to snowy themes, primarily featuring a cold palette of white, blue and purple. This Skin type is available for Christmas Toons {{Small|({{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, {{CI|Coal|name=true}}, {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, & {{CI|Rudie|name=true}})}} and {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}. The Skin Pack containing the Skins are only available during the Christmas Event.
**[[Spring-Time Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to spring themes, primarily featuring a palette of white, green, and pink. This Skin type is available for Easter Toons {{Small|({{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, {{CI|Eggson|name=true}}, & {{CI|Flyte|name=true}})}} and {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}. The Skin Pack containing the Skins are only available during the Easter Event.
**[[Spooky-Time Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to spooky themes, primarily featuring a palette of pink, purple, yellow, and orange. This Skin type is available for Halloween Toons {{Small|({{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}, {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}, {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}}, & {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}})}} and {{CI|Connie|name=true}}. The Skin Pack containing the Skins are only available during the Halloween Event.
**[[Queens of Mischief Cosmetic Pack]]: Skins related to music themes, primarily featuring a palette of purple and green. This Skin type is available for Halloween Toons {{Small|(Eclipse, Gourdy, Ribecca, & Soulvester)}} and Connie. The Skin Pack containing the Skins are only available during the Halloween Event.
*[[Code]] Skins: These Skins are only obtainable via Codes. Currently, only one Skin is obtained through Codes, that being the {{Skin|Research-mobile|toon=[[Rodger]]}}, whose Code is still available and will be available every April 1st. {{Skin|Colorful April|toon=[[Yatta]]}} used to only obtainable through a Code, but was changed to a [[Dyle's Store]] Skin on April 1st, 2026.
*{{Skin|Golden}} Skins: Skins that often feature special trails, particles and/or effects that make them more unique from the other Skins. These are obtained through completing certain types of Quests while using a certain Toon or doing certain actions. As of now, only the Holiday Toons, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, [[Finn]], {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, {{CI|Sprout|name=true}},  {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}, and [[Astro]] (currently ongoing) have Golden Skins, however, every Toon will be getting one when their [[Toon of the Week]] arrives.

