==Trivia==
*There are a total of {{SkinAmount}} Skins in the game, including Skins from [[Gamepasses]], [[Masteries]], [[Events]], [[Collabs]], and [[Codes]].
*{{CI|Sprout|name=true}} has the most Skins in-game as of [[Changelog|v0.22.1]], with eleven (ten without the default), with those being his {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|Salted Caramel}}, {{Skin|Star-Time}}, {{Skin|ChocoBerry}}, {{Skin|Berry Beast}}, {{Skin|Sugary Shortcake}}, {{Skin|Tasty Carrot}}, {{Skin|Chef}}, {{Skin|Golden Berry}}, and {{Skin|Tenderheart Bear}}.
**{{CI|Looey|name=true}}, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}, and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} have the second most Skins in-game, with all of them having ten skins (nine excluding the default).
***Looey with his {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|Dapperly Festive}}, {{Skin|Swirling Mix Up}}, {{Skin|Show-Time}}, {{Skin|Creepy Clown}}, {{Skin|Marching Band}}, {{Skin|Funny Bunny}}, {{Skin|Pastel Patterns}}, and {{Skin|Scribbled Prank}};
***Yatta with her {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|Colorful April}}, {{Skin|Blossom Buddy}}, {{Skin|Show-Time}}, {{Skin|Guess What I Eat}}, {{Skin|Choco Cones}}, {{Skin|Infected Candy}}, {{Skin|Crinkled Confetti}}, and {{Skin|Notta Phase}};
****Yatta used to be the sole Toon with the most Skins for a while, tying with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} in v0.10, outranking him in v0.11-v0.13, tying with him, Razzle & Dazzle, and {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} in the updates in v0.14, and was briefly deranked in v0.17.1-v0.17.15. She was finally deranked in v0.21.1 by Sprout.
***Gourdy with his {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|Midnight Sleeper}}, {{Skin|Crinkling Leaves}}, {{Skin|Lost Prince}}, {{Skin|Fresh Fall}}, {{Skin|Spooky-Time}}, {{Skin|Golden}}, {{Skin|QoM}}, and {{Skin|Unearthed Spirit}}.
***Razzle & Dazzle with their {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|SeaFoam}}, {{Skin|Show-Time}}, {{Skin|Radiant Dream}}, {{Skin|Matcha Morning}}, {{Skin|Cozy Christmas}}, {{Skin|Giftwrap and Ribbons}}, {{Skin|Spring Formal}}, and {{Skin|Curious Stranger}}.<!-- Someone write his most skin timeline all i know is he started christmas  -->
***Sprout's high number of Skins is likely due to him getting his [[Toon of the Week]] Skins first, along with a [[Collab]] Skin. Therefore, after the following Toons get their Toon of the Week Skins and other Skins, they could tie with Sprout.
****Additionally, Yatta is missing one [[Event]] Skin, so when she get it, she could derank Sprout.
***In contrast, {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} is the Toon with least Skins in the game, with 4 (3 if excluding the default); his {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin, {{Skin|Villainous Casual}}, and {{Skin|Toxic Experiment}}.
*Obtaining Skins was formerly a gacha system; you would buy a Red Ticket for 300 {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}, and it would randomly roll a Skin for you. Upon obtaining a duplicate Skin this way, it would be added to a counter of 5. Rolling 5 duplicates would guarantee that the next roll wouldn't be a duplicate.
**This was changed a few hours after release, making it so you could directly buy Skins for 1000 Ichor instead. This price was then reduced shortly after, and now you can buy Skins for 600 Ichor each.
***This change was made because Roblox bans gacha systems in certain countries like Belgium due to their laws, which made a decent amount of the player base unable to get Skins at all.
**There used to be a [[gamepass]] that would auto-roll Skins for you. However, it was very quickly removed because of the gacha system's removal.
***After the announcement of the gamepass' removal, [[Qwelver]] confirmed that people who had bought the gamepass before its deletion would instead get one exclusive Skin for each of the non-[[Event]] {{Type|Main}} Toons, with the Skins matching a certain, space focused theme.
****This became the [[Star-Time Cosmetic Pack]], which costs 200 {{Robux}} in [[Dandy's Store]] and [[Dyle's Store]].
*[[Looey]], [[Gourdy]], {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, {{CI|Eggson|name=true}}, {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, and {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} all have Skins that alter their posture and/or animations. The possible reason for some of these cases, is to accommodate for bigger clothes, such as dresses, in order to reduce clipping. It may also be done to simulate tighter clothing.
**All of Looey's Skins cause his feet to stay on the ground, rather than bounce in his idle animation when he released.
**Gourdy's {{Skin|Midnight Sleeper}} Skin causes his arms to be held higher up, rather than by his side in his idle and walking animations.
**Brusha's {{Skin|Scary Stylish}} Skin causes her posture to be upright rather than slanted.
**Bobette's {{Skin|Holly Lace}}, {{Skin|Snow-Time}}, and {{Skin|Golden Bauble}} Skins cause her head to simply shake side-to-side in her running animation, as opposed to her whole body and head tilting while shaking. Her arms are also lower in her walking animation.
**Toodles' {{Skin|Festive Dress}} and {{Skin|Tea Party Guest}} cause her arms to be held higher up in her idle and walking animations.
**Brightney's {{Skin|Cozy Lighting}} Skin causes her arms to be held higher up in all animations.
**Shrimpo's {{Skin|Fairy Godmother}} and {{Skin|Bundled Up}} Skins cause his arms to be held higher up in all animations.
**Eggson's {{Skin|Still Hip}} Skin changes his second idle animation to spinning his "cane", instead a skateboard, rather than fixing his glasses' posture.
***This is the first and currently only Skin to give a completely new idle animation to a Toon.
**Cocoa's {{Skin|Wildberry Delight}} and {{Skin|Spring-Time}} Skins cause her arms to be held higher up in her idle and running animations. Her hands are held to her belly further apart in her walking animation as well.
**Bassie's {{Skin|Sunflower Patch}}, {{Skin|Spring-Time}}, and {{Skin|Egg Hunting}} Skins cause her walking animation to be slower, almost as if she is gliding. Her arms also are held more outward in her running animation, appearing livelier.
**Rodger's {{Skin|Research-mobile}} Skin causes his arms to rest on top of the costume in all of his animations, he also extracts with his left hand while standing tall.
***This is the first, and currently only Skin to completely alter a Toon's extracting animation.
*There are many pairs/groups of Skins that were designed to match with other [[Toons]], with examples being:
**{{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, and [[Sprout]] ({{Skin|Sweet Roll}}, {{Skin|Sugar Cookie}}, and {{Skin|Sugary Shortcake}} respectively), which have a pastel pink, blue, and white color palette. They have frilled clothes, as well as pastel pink and blue sprinkles on white frosting.
***Cosmo and Sprout have some more matching pairs of Skins, with one caramel pair ({{Skin|Caramel Drizzle}} and {{Skin|Salted Caramel}}), one swapped pair ({{Skin|Berry Roll}} and {{Skin|ChocoBerry}}), one {{wp|Frankenstein}}-themed pair ({{Skin|Dessertful Scientist}} and {{Skin|Berry Beast}}), and one carrot themed pair ({{Skin|Carrot Cake}} and {{Skin|Tasty Carrot}}).
****You can argue that Vee's {{Skin|Zapped Creation}} Skin fits in with Cosmo and Sprout's Frankenstein pair, being inspired by either Frankenstein's monster or the Bride of Frankenstein.
****You can also argue that Looey fits into Cosmo and Sprout's carrot pair with his {{Skin|Funny Bunny}} Skin.
**All of the base {{Type|Main}} Toons ({{Skin|Star-Time}} Skins), which have a blue, yellow, and white color palette. They have a possible clothing theme of space, galaxy or social hangouts, with white sparkles and multicolored trails that feature celestial objects.
**The [[Christmas Toons]] and Cosmo ({{Skin|Snow-Time}} Skins), which have a white, purple, teal, and gray color palette. They have a possible clothing theme of ice skating, with moving textures and trails with a gradient of a similar color palette, featuring snowflakes.
**All [[Event Toons]] and previous [[Toon of the Week]]s ({{Skin|Golden|toon=[[Quest]]}} Skins), which have a red, gold, yellow, orange, and white color palette, alongside golden crowns with red gems and golden sparkle trails.
***Because of this, you can argue that the Christmas Toons, Easter Toons, and Halloween Toons all match with each other, as well as base game Toons with Golden Skins.
**{{CI|Finn|name=true}} and [[Shrimpo]] ({{Skin|Ice Fisher}} and {{Skin|Bundled Up}} respectively), both of which have a yellow, red, and green color palette. They have a clothing theme of ice fishing gear and have trails featuring splashing water.
**[[Rodger]] and [[Toodles]] ({{Skin|List Maker}} and {{Skin|Little Helper}} respectively), both of which have a green, red, and black color palette. They have a clothing theme of Santa and Christmas elves and have yellow sparkle trails.
**{{CI|Blot|name=true}}, [[Looey]], [[Razzle & Dazzle]], {{CI|Vee|name=true}}, and [[Yatta]] ({{Skin|Show-Time}} Skins), which have a royal blue, dark teal, yellow, orange, and red color palette. The Circus Troupe & Vee all have white face paint, Dazzle has white blush, and Razzle already has a white mask. They have a clothing theme of circus performers (or in Vee's case, a ringmaster), with white & red sparkles and multicolored trails featuring circus tents & tickets.
***The Circus Troupe also have their own set of Skins, ({{Skin|Fancy Frosting}}, {{Skin|Pastel Patterns}}, and {{Skin|Crinkled Confetti}}) which have a white, pink, lilac, and pastel blue color palette. Looey also has pastel yellow and pastel green, with Blot having the yellow, and Yatta having the green. They all incorporate bow ties or hair bows into their outfits. They have a possible clothing theme of parties, with pastel colored confetti trails.
****You could also count {{Skin|Sanguine Silence}}, {{Skin|Creepy Clown}}, and {{Skin|Infected Candy}} (Blot, Looey, and Yatta's Skins respectively) due to their shared inspirations of popular monsters or horror figures (a killer clown, vampire, and zombie). They also have a possible reference to the use of fake blood in Halloween costumes (or in this case, fake [[Ichor]]), with Looey and Yatta's Skins having black Ichor-like splatters or dripping marks. Although Blot's Skin doesn't directly have fake Ichor, vampires are notorious for drinking blood, with costumes of such tending to reference this.
**{{CI|Flutter|name=true}} and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} ({{Skin|Rosy Maple Moth}} and {{Skin|Luna Moth}} respectively), which have unique color palettes each inspired by real-life moth species, being the {{wp|rosy maple moth}} and {{wp|luna moth}} species. The wings of the Skins are larger than their average Skins and have flamboyant patterns like that of their eponymous moth species.
**The [[Easter]] Toons and Flutter ({{Skin|Spring-Time}} Skins), which have a white, pink, and matcha green color palette. With the exception of Eggson, they have white freckles on their cheeks, with the butterfly siblings also having freckles on their wings. They have a possible clothing theme of picnics or outings, with matcha green glitter-like sparkles, purple & pink flowers, and yellow trails featuring flowers & leaves.
**{{CI|Goob|name=true}} and {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} have matching Easter Skins ({{Skin|Garden Blossoms|name=true}} and {{Skin|Garden Bouquet|name=true}} respectively), which have a green, pink, and brown color palette. They have a theme of gardens, with pink and reddish flowers, with leafy elements on them. They additionally have two pairs of whiskers on their cheeks.
***You could also count their {{Skin|Neapolitan}} and {{Skin|Rainbow Sherbet}} Skins due to both Skins being themed after frozen desserts, as well as featuring a tricolor design inspired by their eponymous ice cream/sherbet flavors respectively.
**The [[Halloween Toons]] and Connie ({{Skin|Spooky-Time}} Skins), which have a pink, purple, yellow, and orange color palette. They mostly have a theme of Halloween beasts, with saturated colors all over. They additionally have pink & orange spider web particles and moving textures.
***The five Toons also have the {{Skin|QoM}} Skins, which have a green, purple, black, and white color palette. The theme is based on the "Queens of Mischief" band, with Connie, Eclipse, & Ribecca being the singers and instrumentalists (keytarist, guitarist, and bassist in no confirmed order), Gourdy being a drummer, and Soulvester being a bouncer. The specific fashion style appears to be inspired by aspects of glam rock, rave, and punk outfits. They additionally have purple, green, & white music note particles and music sheet trails.
***Additionally, Connie and {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}} could match with their {{Skin|Ghastly Glow}} and {{Skin|Haunted Flame}} Skins, being themed around purplish or pink flames, and having dripping black liquid, possibly resembling Ichor.
**{{CI|Boxten|name=true}} and {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} could have thematically matching Skins, with {{Skin|Quiet Caroler}} and {{Skin|Confident Caroler}} both being based on Christmas carolers, and sharing white, green, and red in their color palettes.
**There's a tendency for related [[Toons]] to have at least one matching Skin with each other. The same can be said for some established groups of Toons (such as the Circus Troupe), however not all of them have matching Skins (such as the Book Club). This may change in the future, but is not currently confirmed.
*{{Skin|Special Spaghetti|toon=[[Goob]]}}, {{Skin|Ebony Detective|toon=[[Rodger]]}}, {{Skin|Dapperly Festive|toon=[[Looey]]}}, {{Skin|Infected Candy|toon=[[Yatta]]}}, {{Skin|Choco Cones Yatta}}, {{Skin|Brisk Breeze|toon=[[Connie]]}}, {{Skin|Sparkling Snow|toon={{CI|Glisten|name=true}}}}, {{Skin|Chilly Penguin|toon=[[Blot]]}}, {{Skin|Funny Bunny|toon=[[Looey]]}}, and {{Skin|Tea Party Guest|toon=[[Toodles]]}} are the only known Skins that were not designed by [[Qwel]].
